      "customfield_10001" : "1_*:*_1_*:*_14935_*|*_3_*:*_1_*:*_49053345837_*|*_5_*:*_1_*:*_0",
      "customfield_10012" : "0|i0031j:",
      "customfield_10300" : "{}",
      "description" : {
         "content" : [
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "This MAY be the reason for the subtle memory bugs on the ARM BLKQCL device.",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "I've seen some (vague - I dont understand) indications that x86 has memory strongly ",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "ordered and arm - maybe - not.",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "That could explain why I havent seen the valgrind or memory corruptions issues on x86.",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "Or it could be soemthing else.",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "marks" : [
                        {
                           "attrs" : {
                              "href" : "http://www.boost.org/doc/libs/1_54_0/doc/html/atomic/usage_examples.html#boost_atomic.usage_examples.example_spinlock"
                           },
                           "type" : "link"
                        }
                     ],
                     "text" : "http://www.boost.org/doc/libs/1_54_0/doc/html/atomic/usage_examples.html#boost_atomic.usage_examples.example_spinlock",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : " says to use memory_order_acquire.",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "Unclear wht todo on unlock.",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "But I THINK the right thing is to use std::memory_order_seq_cst on lock and do nothing on unlock.",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "At least test that for a bit.",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            }
         ],
         "type" : "doc",
         "version" : 1
      },
